{
  "_comment": "Pack-EV model for the sets /tools/pack-ev covers. Rates are per pack, per slot, quoted as \"1 in N\" (`odds`) or as a decimal (`chance`); each slot resolves to exactly one outcome, and the outcome that names neither takes whatever the named rates leave. Slot placement follows the pull-rate count linked in each set's `source`: TCGplayer's article where one exists, a community count where it doesn't yet. `specialPacks` are god and demigod packs: at their own rate a pack keeps `keepSlots` and replaces every other slot with `draws` — named cards (`cards`), one group of named cards (`oneOf`), or uniform draws from a pool (`random`). Card pools and named cards resolve against the set's TCGCSV group at build time, plus any `reprintGroupIds` (subsets TCGplayer lists as their own group, like the 30th Celebration Classic Collection); variant products (anything TCGplayer names with a parenthetical) only join a pool that names their `pattern`. Bulk rates are Safari Zone Collectibles' posted buylist; `threshold` is the market price a card has to clear before it counts as more than bulk.",
